<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: no AIF gap entry starts on nop padding (part of
    `option aif`).

    Issue:      kuna GH-299 - aif plants entries that are not function starts
                on large i386 PEs; most of the non-start ones are the nop runs
                in front of Wine's relay thunks.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the AIF gap-walk probe
                (`analyzers/aif/kuna_aifnoppad.rs`).
    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Both passes clear
    it and loads `aifnoppad_pe_i386.exe` (source `aifnoppad_pe_i386.asm`
    beside it): five called stubs open with nine nops, so `nop, nop` is a
    shared prologue fingerprint; eight nops pad from `relay`'s `ret 4` to the
    called `hot` at 0x401230; `dead` at 0x401239 opens with `mov edi,edi`
    straight after a return; `lone` at 0x40124c sits behind six nops with a
    prologue nothing else shares.  Neither `dead` nor `lone` is referenced.

    Before the filler rule the inventory listed sub_401228 and sub_401248,
    both on nops.
    Pass 1 (`mode aggressive`) lists neither, lists `lone` at its own
    address, and keeps `dead`: `mov edi,edi` is not padding.
    Pass 2 (`mode aggressive`, `option aif off`) shows `dead` and `lone` are
    the gap walk's own finds.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/aifnoppad_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>mode aggressive</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/aifnoppad_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>mode aggressive</com>
  <com>option aif off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-AIFNOPPAD #1: hot is a function in both passes" min="2" max="2">0x401230 sub_401230</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-AIFNOPPAD #2: the padding in front of hot is never a function" min="0" max="0">0x401228 sub_401228</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-AIFNOPPAD #3: the padding in front of lone is never a function" min="0" max="0">0x401248 sub_401248</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-AIFNOPPAD #4: lone is found at its own address by the gap walk" min="1" max="1">0x40124c sub_40124c</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-AIFNOPPAD #5: the mov edi,edi entry after a return stays an AIF function" min="1" max="1">0x401239 sub_401239</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
